+# eye(studio): human-eye QA cycle III — 2026-10-28 — signup funnel end-to-end (register works, same-credentials login 401 server-side), 320 px small-mobile sweep (first sub-375 px evidence, F-4 worsens), deploy-mirror build skew (Pages pre-#1782 SW v4 empty cache vs Vercel v5 6 cached assets). Zero duplicates of #1783/#1799/#1797/#1808.
+
+Human-eye role cycle (2026-10-28 07:45+08 dispatch, Job 477792). Complements the four prior studio-QA evidence sets rather than re-treading them: #1783 (landing FCP + tap targets at 390 px), #1797 (cold-FCP distribution + first LCP/CLS), #1799 (F-1…F-6 at 375 px: login breakage, chat leak, contrast, selector clip, login validation, error copy), and #1808 (tablet 768 px, mirror parity snapshot, auth 405-vs-404 specificity, cold-FCP corroboration). This cycle covers the dimensions none of them touched: **the signup funnel journey end-to-end** (prior cycles only tested login and guest chat), **the 320 px small-mobile class** (first sub-375 px evidence), and **the deployed service-worker/build state of both mirrors after #1782** (runtime asset-cache fix landed in main ~06:00+08; deploy-state unknown until now). **Report-only** — no code changed.
+
+**Target:** `https://supremeai-studio.pages.dev` (primary) and `https://supremeai-studio.vercel.app` (mirror).
+**Probe window:** 2026-10-27 23:50–2026-10-28 00:35 UTC (2026-10-28 07:50–08:35 +08).
+**Conditions (no synthetic claims):** agent-browser headless Chrome; isolated fresh sessions; 1280×800 / 320×568 emulated viewports; network **unthrottled**; **no Lighthouse/Web Vitals score claimed**; zero-credential except one explicitly disclosed throwaway account (see Never-do register); MCP Control Tower handshake healthy at cycle start (session cb07c80a, bridge queue 20 open WOs).
+
+## 1. NEW dimension A — signup funnel journey, end to end (first signup evidence in the series)
+
+Prior cycles tested the login form (#1799 F-1/F-5) and guest chat (#1799 journeys) but never the registration funnel. Full journey at 1280×800 on the Pages host:
+
+| Step | Result |
+|---|---|
+| Landing → "Create Free Account" → `/register` | Form renders: Full name / Email address / Password / Confirm password, "Create account", disabled "Continue with Google (coming soon)" |
+| Empty submit | **Bengali alert "দয়া করে সব ফিল্ড পূরণ করুন।"**, `role=alert`, visible, **no network request fired** — client-side guard works (contrast: login form F-5 had zero feedback) |
+| Invalid email + mismatched passwords | Same generic "fill all fields" alert; no wire call |
+| Valid email + mismatched passwords | **Specific English alert "Passwords do not match."** — specific per-field feedback exists |
+| Valid email + matching strong password | **`POST https://supremeai-api-ulw0.onrender.com/api/v1/auth/register → 200`** → redirect **`/workspace`**; workspace renders fully (sidebar, Chat/Profile/Settings nav, model combobox, theme toggle, command palette); **zero console errors** |
+
+**The register client targets the Render gateway origin — not the static host.** This is exactly the fix path #1799's F-1 proposed for login ("point the auth client at the API gateway origin, as the working `/api/config/*` calls already do"). Registration proves the gateway auth surface itself works and that one auth client in this same app is wired correctly. **The login client is the outlier, not the gateway.**
+
+### F-A · CRITICAL (refines #1799 F-1) — register→login roundtrip broken server-side: same credentials rejected 401; accounts lock out on second visit
+
+After the successful register (200, auto-session to `/workspace`), the session was cleared and login attempted **with the exact same fresh credentials**:
+
+- `POST https://supremeai-api-ulw0.onrender.com/api/v1/auth/login` → **HTTP 401**.
+- **Direct gateway curl with the same credentials reproduces independently**: `{"detail":"Invalid email or password"}` HTTP 401 — the rejection is **server-side credential verification**, not a client payload/origin defect.
+- **Supersedes #1799 F-1's "password auth request never fires"**: with real registered credentials the password login request DOES fire, and to the **correct gateway origin**. F-1's proposed fix path (re-point the auth client at the gateway) applies **only to the passkey lane** (re-verified unchanged this cycle: passkey `login/options` → 405 pages.dev / 404 vercel.app). The password lane needs a **server-side** fix (register↔login credential verification/hashing mismatch, or an undisclosed verification gate — no verification UI was shown at register; the app went straight to an authenticated workspace).
+- Net user impact: **you can create an account but never sign back in with it.** The post-register auto-session masks the defect at first run; the lockout appears on the next visit. UI response to the 401 is a visible toast — see F-B.
+
+### F-B · LOW (new) — post-401 toast copy is retry-oriented for an unfixable-from-client defect
+
+After the 401, the UI shows: **"🔑 Invalid credentials. Check your email/password and try again.🔍 Check connection"** — instructing the user to re-check credentials that are provably correct (curl proves the server rejects them) and to check a connection that is healthy. A user with valid credentials will retry indefinitely against a server-side defect. Recorded as copy/UX evidence for the F-1 fixer lane; the emoji-prefixed combined text is also a minor rendering quirk worth normalizing when the auth surface is touched.
+
+### Minor datums (evidence, not filed as defects)
+
+- `GET https://supremeai-api-ulw0.onrender.com/api/preferences/default/stream` → **404** immediately after the successful register + `/workspace` redirect (single occurrence, OPTIONS 200, no crash, workspace unaffected). Datum for the preferences-stream lane.
+- **Mixed-language alerts in the same form**: generic empty-fields alert in Bengali, specific password-mismatch alert in English. The site ships Hind Siliguri (Bengali coverage confirmed in #1799), so Bengali is a supported locale — but per-error language mixing inside one funnel is inconsistent; pick one policy.
+- Register form inputs carry `aria-invalid=null` even after a failed submit (same pattern #1799's F-5 flagged on login); the `role=alert` announcement partially compensates.
+
+## 2. NEW dimension B — 320 px small-mobile sweep (first sub-375 px evidence in the series)
+
+Prior mobile evidence stops at 375 px (#1799) and 390 px (#1783). 320×568 (iPhone SE 1st-gen class) was never probed:
+
+| Check @320×568 | Result |
+|---|---|
+| Horizontal page overflow (`/`, `/login`, `/register`, `/chat`) | **PASS — `scrollWidth == clientWidth == 320` on all four routes** (no page-level horizontal scroll) |
+| `/chat` model selector | **F-4 worsens at 320**: selector measures **398 px wide, right edge at 590 px on a 320 px viewport** (≈84 % of the control off-screen); its toolbar row reports `scrollWidth=561` vs `clientWidth=262`. #1808 bounded F-4 to the "375 px class" — this cycle extends the mapped range: the `select.flex-1` min-width defect also hits 320 px and **more severely** (partial clip at 375 → majority clip at 320). Evidence only; not re-filed |
+| Landing CTAs | "Try Live Guest Chat" **272×48 px**, "Create Free Account" **272×50 px** — full-width stacked, PASS (desktop-navbar Sign In/Get Started correctly `display:none` at 320) |
